      "flagged": true,
      "answer": "Objective: Register a custom route in Drupal 10 to return rendered output from a custom module.\n\nTo register a custom route in Drupal 10, you need to define a new route in `your_module.routing.yml` file.\n\n```yml\nyour_module.your_route:\n  path: '/hello'\n  defaults:\n    _controller: '\\Drupal\\your_module\\Controller\\YourController::yourMethod'\n    _title: 'Hello World'\n```\n\nIn the above code, replace `your_module` and `your_route` with your actual module name and route name. The `YourController` class should implement a method named `yourMethod` that returns the rendered output.\n\n```php\nnamespace Drupal\\your_module\\Controller;\n\nuse Drupal\\Core\\Controller\\ControllerBase;\n\nclass YourController extends ControllerBase {\n\n  public function yourMethod() {\n    return $this->render('your_template');\n  }\n\n}\n```\n\nIn the above code, replace `your_template` with your actual template file name.\n\nYou also need to clear the Drupal cache after registering the new route.\n\nVersion notes: This solution is for Drupal 10. Please adjust the code according to your needs.",
